  "final_message": "I didn't do a straight rename. `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside the old `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass. I didn't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.\n\n**Why not a rename:** ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` in other repos. Changes must be additive, and renames go through deprecation. Dropping `totalCents` and `placedAt` outright would break those consumers.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `OrderPlaced` now has `amountCents` and `createdAt`. The old `totalCents` and `placedAt` stay, marked `@deprecated`, and carry the same values. `schemaVersion` is still 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **`test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts`:** the tests now check the new fields as well as the old ones.\n\n**Not changed:** the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the other API responses still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires web-storefront compatibility, and you only asked about the event.\n\n**To finish the rename:** the old fields can be removed once billing-service and analytics-ingest have moved to the new names. That needs a deprecation notice to those teams and probably a `schemaVersion` bump. I haven't done either.",
